One Mines' End variant *may* have a loadstone in a corner next
to undiggabe walls.  Of course, a randomly generated loadstone
may appear anywhere, including in a corner, and if the level is
undiggable (and Mines' End isn't the only place this may be
true), the trick with kicking can't be used.  (I've had this
happen in the Valley of the Dead, for example.)  But otherwise:
only one Mines' End variant has a guaranteed loadstone.  It may
be in one of seven places, only two of which won't allow
kicking.  And in these seven places, the only other stone which
can be mistaken for a loadstone is the luckstone, so if you've
found the luckstone in one of the other places, then the gray
stone must be a loadstone (and vice versa).  So the only real
problem would be if the luckstone and the loadstone are *both*
in the two places where you can't kick; this should occur less
than 5% of the time.

